## Clusterwide default deny

By default the app creates a `default-deny-all` policy in each namespace listed in `denyByDefault.namespaces`.
Setting `denyByDefault.clusterWide.enabled: true` replaces those with one `CiliumClusterwideNetworkPolicy`,
`default-deny-all-namespaces`, that denies all traffic of every namespace, `kube-system` and `giantswarm` included.
The switch is off by default and is opted into per cluster. It is independent of `denyByDefault.enabled`.

- **Namespace opt-out.** A namespace carrying the label `policy.giantswarm.io/default-deny: "false"` is not covered.
  Namespaces without the label are denied. Do not label `kube-system` or `giantswarm` with it.
- **Clusterwide DNS allow.** `denyByDefault.clusterWide.allowDNS.enabled: true` adds `allow-dns-all-namespaces`,
  an L4-only egress allow to CoreDNS, node-local DNS cache and kube-dns for every covered namespace.
  Enable it in the same change as `clusterWide.enabled`, or give every customer namespace a DNS allow first.
  Otherwise DNS breaks the moment the deny lands.
- **Rollback.** First opt the affected namespace out with the label above. If that is not enough,
  set `denyByDefault.clusterWide.enabled: false`, which restores the per-namespace policies.

Standard allows and allow labels come in a later change (giantswarm/roadmap#4376).

